{"id":"kara","title":"The Last Light of Kara Island","level":"B1","scenes":[{"title":"The Lighthouse Keeper","text":"Every summer, twelve-year-old Leyla visited her grandfather, Rauf, who was the keeper of an old lighthouse on Kara Island. The island was small and quiet, and the only sounds were the wind and the waves.","img":"scene1.webp","fx":["leaves"]},{"title":"It Is a Promise","text":"Leyla loved climbing the narrow stairs to the top, where the huge lamp turned slowly all night. Her grandfather always said that the light was not just a lamp. “It is a promise,” he told her. “It tells every sailor that someone is watching over them.”","img":"scene2.webp","fx":["leaves"]},{"title":"The Storm","text":"One evening, a terrible storm came from the north. The sky turned black, and the rain hit the windows like stones. Suddenly, the electricity went off and the great lamp stopped turning. Grandfather Rauf tried to start the old generator, but it was broken. Far out at sea, Leyla saw the small lights of a fishing boat moving towards the dangerous rocks.","img":"scene3.webp","fx":["rain","flash"]},{"title":"The Old Oil Lamp","text":"Leyla remembered an old oil lamp that she had seen in the storage room. She ran down the stairs, found the lamp and a box of matches, and carried them to the top of the tower.","img":"scene4.webp","fx":["glow"]},{"title":"The Last Light","text":"Her hands were shaking, but she managed to light it. Then she held the lamp in front of the big mirror, and its light became bright enough to reach the sea. Slowly, the boat changed its direction and moved away from the rocks.","img":"scene5.webp","fx":["rain","glow"]},{"title":"A Brave Heart","text":"The next morning, the fishermen came to the lighthouse to thank them. The captain told Leyla that without her light, his whole crew could have died. Grandfather Rauf put his hand on her shoulder and smiled proudly. Leyla realised that being brave does not mean having no fear. It means doing the right thing even when you are afraid.","img":"scene6.webp","fx":["leaves"]}],"audio":"narration.mp3","timing":{"words":[["Every",0.06,0.57],["summer",0.57,0.92],["twelve-year-old",1.16,2.15],["Leyla",2.15,2.68],["visited",2.68,3.44],["her",3.44,3.75],["grandfather",3.75,4.51],["Rauf",4.51,4.82],["who",5.2,5.46],["was",5.46,5.73],["the",5.73,5.99],["keeper",5.99,6.46],["of",6.46,6.72],["an",6.72,6.99],["old",6.99,7.25],["lighthouse",7.25,7.71],["on",7.71,7.98],["Kara",7.98,8.44],["Island",8.44,8.9],["The",9.76,10.11],["island",10.11,10.72],["was",10.72,11.07],["small",11.07,11.42],["and",11.42,11.77],["quiet",11.77,12.12],["and",12.3,12.59],["the",12.59,12.88],["only",12.88,13.39],["sounds",13.39,13.68],["were",13.68,13.97],["the",13.97,14.26],["wind",14.26,14.55],["and",14.55,14.84],["the",14.84,15.13],["waves",15.13,15.64],["Leyla",16.52,16.97],["loved",16.97,17.43],["climbing",17.43,17.88],["the",17.88,18.14],["narrow",18.14,18.6],["stairs",18.6,18.86],["to",18.86,19.12],["the",19.12,19.38],["top",19.38,19.64],["where",20.04,20.36],["the",20.36,20.68],["huge",20.68,21],["lamp",21,21.32],["turned",21.32,21.88],["slowly",21.88,22.44],["all",22.44,22.76],["night",22.76,23.08],["Her",23.68,23.95],["grandfather",23.95,24.62],["always",24.62,25.09],["said",25.09,25.36],["that",25.36,25.63],["the",25.63,25.9],["light",25.9,26.17],["was",26.17,26.44],["not",26.44,26.71],["just",26.71,26.98],["a",26.98,27.25],["lamp",27.25,27.52],["It",28.44,28.76],["is",28.76,29.07],["a",29.07,29.39],["promise",29.39,29.93],["he",29.93,30.25],["told",30.25,30.56],["her",30.56,30.88],["It",31.06,31.33],["tells",31.33,31.61],["every",31.61,32.29],["sailor",32.29,32.77],["that",32.77,33.04],["someone",33.04,33.52],["is",33.52,33.79],["watching",33.79,34.27],["over",34.27,34.75],["them",34.75,35.02],["One",36,36.3],["evening",36.3,37.04],["a",37.04,37.33],["terrible",37.33,38.07],["storm",38.07,38.37],["came",38.37,38.67],["from",38.67,38.96],["the",38.96,39.26],["north",39.26,39.56],["The",40.04,40.3